📘 Common Causes of Hardware Failure – Quick Summary

1. Mechanical Causes

  - Wear and tear of moving parts (HDDs, fans)
  - Physical damage (dropping, impact)
  - Improper installation (forcing components, misaligned cables)

  Prevention:

    - Switch to SSDs (no moving parts)
    - Handle devices carefully
    - Regularly check cable connections

2. Electrical Causes

  - Power surges/spikes
  - Overheating (dust buildup)
  - Short circuits

  Prevention:
  
    - Use surge protectors
    - Use UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply)
    - Clean dust regularly
    - Keep liquids away from electronics

3. Environmental Causes

  - Extreme temperatures
  - High humidity/moisture
  - Dust and debris

  - Prevention:
  
    - Keep systems in climate-controlled environments
    - Clean regularly
    - Use humidity-controlled storage for sensitive components

4. Manufacturing Defects

  - Cannot be prevented – only detected
  - Detection: Monitoring tools (e.g., Check Disk for drives)
  - Solution: Replacement (hopefully under warranty)

5. Software-Induced Failures (Rare)

  - Usually caused by faulty monitoring software
  - Example: CPU temperature monitoring fails → CPU overheats
  
  - Prevention:
  
    - Monitor system temperatures
    - Check system logs
    - Perform regular backups

6. Best Practices for Longevity

  - Measure	Purpose
  - Regular backups	Data safety
  - Monitor temperatures	Prevent overheating
  - Check system logs	Detect errors early
  - Replace aging components	Prevent failures
  - Keep systems up-to-date	Ensure stability
